      "writtenOn": "2021-05-28T01:27:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Currently S is 10000. I want to make sure new algorithm tests can be covered on cuttlefish, whose first sdk version is 31.\n\nI expect on cuttlefish, all new algorithms are mandatory and I want the following code block can verify that and can throw if cuttlefish does not support any new algorithm\n\n```\n        // Verify all mandatory algorithms are supported\n        for (Entry\u003cString, Integer\u003e entry : algoToRequiredFirstSdk.entrySet()) {\n            if (Build.VERSION.FIRST_SDK_INT \u003e\u003d entry.getValue()) {\n                assertTrue(\n                        \"Fail to support \" + entry.getKey(),\n                        supportedAlgos.contains(entry.getKey()));\n            }\n        }\n```\n\nOn the other side, if we use S in the map, than on the new algorithms, \"if (Build.VERSION.FIRST_SDK_INT \u003e\u003d entry.getValue())\" will return false which means the new algorithms are not expected to be mandatory and then we will skip the \"assertTrue\" check.",
